{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Well they [F#m]blew up the [A]chicken man in [D]Philly last [A]night
and they blew up his house too
Down on the boardwalk, they're ready for a fight
gonna see what them racket boys can do    (riff over “can do”)
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Now there's trouble busing in, from outta state
and the D.A. can't get no relief
Gonna be a rumble out on the promenade
and the [F#m]gambling commissioners [A]hanging on, by the [E]skin of his teeth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Everything dies baby that's a fact
But maybe everything that dies someday comes back
Put your makeup on, fix your hair up pretty and
Meet me tonight, in Atlantic City
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Well I got a job and tried to put my money away
But I got the kind of debt no honest man can pay
So I drew what I had from the Central Trust
And I bought us two tickets on that Coast City bus
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Solo into BRIDGE
Now our [D]luck may have died, and our [F#m]love may be cold
but with [D]you, [E]forever I'll [F#m]stay
Yeah we're [D]going out where, the [F#m]sand turns to gold
[E]so put your stockings on, cause it might get cold
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Solo}
Now I been looking for a job but it's hard to find
There’s winners and losers and I’m south of that line
Well I'm tired of coming out on the losing end
But I talked to a man last night and I'm gonna do a little favor for him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Chorus – tag last line twice and Fade out with solos
{end_of_verse}
